# Husky pre-push hook — refuse to push release tags from a local machine.
#
# Why: the release flow requires tags to be created from inside the
# `Build & Release` workflow, after the preflight (which includes
# `vsce verify-pat`) has succeeded. A hand-pushed `v*` tag would bypass
# that safety net and, because the repo's ruleset makes tags immutable,
# could burn a version number if the workflow later refused to publish.
#
# See `.github/instructions/publish-update-extension.instructions.md`
# and `AGENTS.md` for the full release runbook.
#
# Bypass with `git push --no-verify` if you genuinely need to (e.g. you
# are pushing a non-`v*` tag, or you are the maintainer intentionally
# repairing state after an outage). Contributors should never need this.

# Git passes ref updates on stdin: "<local ref> <local sha> <remote ref> <remote sha>\n"
while read -r local_ref _local_sha remote_ref _remote_sha; do
  case "$remote_ref" in
    refs/tags/v*)
      cat <<EOF >&2
❌ Refusing to push $remote_ref from a local machine.

Release tags (v*) must be created by the 'Build & Release' workflow, not
by hand. Manual tag pushes bypass the VSCE_PAT preflight and, because
the repository ruleset makes tags immutable, can burn a version number
if the Marketplace publish later fails.

To cut a release:
  1. Merge the version bump PR to master.
  2. Verify the PAT: gh workflow run verify-marketplace-auth.yml
  3. Dispatch the release: gh workflow run release.yml -f version=X.Y.Z

See .github/instructions/publish-update-extension.instructions.md for
the full runbook.

If you genuinely need to bypass this check, use:
  git push --no-verify $remote_ref
EOF
      exit 1
      ;;
  esac

  # Non-tag refs (branches) and non-v* tags are fine.
  : "$local_ref"
done

exit 0
